                <pb facs="0441" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg419"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Mr. Favrot</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 2.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-04-15"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 15,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Inclosed I transmit to you sealed letters
                    for each of the Arbitrators appointed under the first Article of the Treaty of
                    Washington, and the British Agent. A copy is inclosed.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to forward the letters and accompanying documents, addressed to
                    Count Sclopis, Mr. Stämpfli, Mr. Adams, Sir Alexander Cockburn, and Lord
                    Tenterden, respectively.</p>
                <p>I have been requested by the Baron d’Itajubá, to take charge of his letter, and I
                    will see that it is duly delivered to him with the documents to which it
                    refers.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. C. B. DAVIS.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
